{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/ReplaceError\/timeout(_:customError:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"customError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"text":")? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Timeout","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuspendingClock","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"duration","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}]}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws before the first element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Example","text":"Example"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["for try await event in serverEvents.timeout(.seconds(30)) {","    handle(event)","}","\/\/ Throws TimeoutError.timedOut if 30 seconds pass without an event"],"type":"codeListing"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customError"},{"type":"text","text":") when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration"},{"type":"text","text":" passes between elements, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any error the upstream throws."}]}],"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock (","type":"text"},{"code":"ContinuousClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SuspendingClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") holds the one thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timer can hold the thread before the upstream runs, then count that wait against it and throw even","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"though elements were ready. A test clock is unaffected.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fails if the sequence goes the given duration without producing an element, measured on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"relatedModules":["_Concurrency"],"name":"Afluent"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"customError"},{"kind":"text","text":": (any "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"},{"kind":"text","text":")?) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Timeout","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SuspendingClock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency15SuspendingClockV"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/TimeoutSequence.swift#L176","fileName":"TimeoutSequence.swift"